cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CHAI, please cite it as below."
title: "CHAI: Cooling Histories via Amortized Inference"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Jiao
    given-names: Ruohong
    email: rjiao@uvic.ca
    affiliation: University of Victoria
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0303-3118
abstract: >-
  CHAI turns apatite fission-track and (U-Th)/He data into thermal histories under a second,
  with calibrated uncertainty. A normalizing flow, trained on millions of synthetic samples,
  draws the posterior of time-temperature paths directly from the measurements. No Monte Carlo
  search runs on your machine. The package also includes exact, differentiable PyTorch ports of
  the fission-track annealing model of Ketcham et al. (2007) and RDAAM of Flowers et al. (2009),
  for posterior-predictive checks against your data.
keywords:
  - thermochronology
  - apatite fission track
  - "(U-Th)/He"
  - thermal history
  - normalizing flow
  - PyTorch
version: 0.15.0
date-released: 2026-10-30
repository-code: https://github.com/jiaor/CHAI
url: https://web.uvic.ca/~rjiao/chai/
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
